# the top row's mute pads as Mix's black keys (app/smk37.c lsmk_mute_up): a tap mutes / unmutes; held: solo while
# held (more held: more soloed), let go: the mutes back; two taps: solo, and it stays; a tap then ends it
wait 300
listen
tap HOME
wait 40
expect mute 0
# a tap: T3 muted, again: unmuted
tappad 2
wait 40
expect mute 4
said MUTED
wait 400
tappad 2
wait 40
expect mute 0
wait 400
# held: T2 soloed while held (every other track muted: the conductor and the throws too), let go: back
pad 1 100
wait 600
expect mute 1021
said SOLO
pad 2 100
wait 600
expect mute 1017
pad 2 0
wait 40
expect mute 1021
pad 1 0
wait 40
expect mute 0
wait 400
# a mute kept under a solo: T5 muted, T2 held, let go: T5 still muted
tappad 4
wait 40
expect mute 16
wait 400
pad 1 100
wait 600
expect mute 1021
pad 1 0
wait 40
expect mute 16
wait 400
tappad 4
wait 400
# two taps: T4 soloed and it stays; a tap: the solo ends
tappad 3
wait 100
tappad 3
wait 40
expect mute 1015
said SOLO
wait 600
expect mute 1015
tappad 6
wait 40
expect mute 0
said SOLO OFF
